---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Record, list, revoke and share decisions about upstream changes

Usage: odx verdict [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add       Record a verdict or mute about a suggestion of `odx suggest`
  list      List verdicts and mutes
  show      Show one verdict
  revoke    Revoke a verdict (recorded, never deleted)
  confirm   Keep a stale verdict after reviewing the changed target code
  upstream  Propose a verdict upstream as an oca-port blacklist entry: written and committed in a worktree of the target branch, pushed and proposed with --open-pr --yes
  sync      Pull and push the private verdict repository
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
